{
 "_about": "Each industry issuer's tags: the words that, standing as whole tokens in a title, say the title is that issuer's (kb/_build_exhibits_review.py issuer_named). Derived once on 2026-11-13 (S648) from every issuer in kb/credentials.json and kb/credential_review_overlay.json: a parenthetical that is one token (ASE, NREMT), and an all-capitals word outside parentheses (IPC); then written down and corrected by hand: generic ones dropped (ROP, HS, DUI, GIS, 'varies'), split ones joined (CAL-OSHA, EC-Council, H&R Block), and brands that sit outside the issuer's short tag added (CAL FIRE, Cal OES, UC ANR, Disney, LEED, Esri, Haas, Unity, LPIC, CLEP, DSST), and, after the review of #3241, each issuer's own credential abbreviations and track names where its real credentials carry no other mark of it (PMI's PfMP and PgMP, Python Institute's PCAP, the Dental Boards' RDA and RDH, NBCOT's COTA, EMSA's EMT and EMR, SFT's certification tracks such as Fire Inspector and Company Officer). The S648 conductor's direction on #3241: the issuer list is finite, so its tags are data, never a pattern. An issuer missing here has no tags: its titles count as named only on the words of its name. Add an issuer when the reference gains one. Two lists per issuer: `tags`, phrases matched in any case (\"SOLIDWORKS\" matches \"SolidWorks\", \"CAL FIRE\" matches \"Cal Fire\"), a trailing \"#\" asking for a level after the phrase (\"Fire Prevention #\" matches \"Fire Prevention 1A\", never \"Fire Prevention Technology\"); and `acronyms`, the issuer's short tags, matched only as written (POST never matches \"Post Production\"). A reference title that several issuers carry names none of them unless the freehand text carries that issuer's acronym (\"SFT Fire Instructor 1\"). NFPA's and Pro Board's bare Fire Inspector, Fire Officer and Firefighter titles stay out on purpose (the S648 conductor, 2026-11-13): several issuers share the bare title, so its card goes to a person.",
 "set_by": "the S648 worker for the conductor, 2026-11-13",
